ly record. Since 2000, Billings has set <strong>72 standing record lows</strong>, fewer than the 106 that chance alone would give, and <strong>128 record highs</strong>, close to the 106 that chance alone would give. The 1980s hold the most record highs of any decade (60). Billings' all-time high is 111\u00b0F, on July 12, 2026.","t_chg":"Billings' nights got warmer. Its days didn't.","p_chg":"Across 91 complete years: Billings' average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.27\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.16 to +0.39), about +2.5\u00b0F since 1935. Billings' average high shows no clear change: +0.15\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.01 to +0.32) that includes zero. It's close, but the range still includes zero.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 6 of 12 months. Highs rose in 3 of 12 months; October fell.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Billings' yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.10 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 14.3 inches a year. The wettest year was 1978 (26.81 in); the driest, 2012 (7.13 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 17 daily record highs, 2 daily record lows"}}